# Read by every build of this repository: on a laptop, in a pull request and in a publish.
# A comment line has to start with '#' in the first column, and every other line is one argument.
#
# How the HTTP transport of Maven Resolver 1.9 (the one in Maven 3.9) repeats a request which a
# server answers with 429 Too Many Requests or 503 Service Unavailable. Only that request is
# repeated, after a pause, and the build goes on. Without these lines the resolver tries three
# more times within 30 seconds, and then the whole build fails.
#
# The pause before repeat n is n times the interval: 15, 30, 45 ... 120 seconds, 9 minutes for
# all 8 repeats. A 'Retry-After' header of the server takes the place of that pause. A pause
# longer than the maximum ends the repeats at once, so a server which asks for more than two
# minutes is not waited for. The longest wait for one request is 8 times 2 minutes.
-Daether.connector.http.retryHandler.count=8
-Daether.connector.http.retryHandler.interval=15000
-Daether.connector.http.retryHandler.intervalMax=120000
-Daether.connector.http.retryHandler.serviceUnavailable=429,503
